A"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-10204926-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>10204926</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="XP" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="JP-3073703-U" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>3073703</doc-number><kind>U</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> </patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1022395A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIGUCHI FUMIKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOBE STEEL LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAJIMA KAZUHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOHJI YUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIGUCHI, FUMIKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KABUSHIKI KAISHA KOBE SEIKO SHO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAJIMA, KAZUHARU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOHJI, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIGUCHI FUMIKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAJIMA KAZUHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOHJI YUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIGUCHI, FUMIKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAJIMA, KAZUHARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOHJI, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A hydraulic control device of a working machine which controls the flow rate and flow direction of the pressure oil discharged from a hydraulic pump (20) through a control valve (27) before the oil is fed to a swing motor (4), characterized by comprising a bleed-off oil path (33) for bleeding off a part of the pressure oil fed to the swing motor (4), a cut valve (36) which is installed in the bleed-off oil path (33) and regulates the bleed-off amount, a controller (42) which controls the cut valve (36) through an electromagnetic proportional valve (37), and pressure sensors (40 and 41) which detect the control input of a swing remote-control valve (39), wherein the controller (42) sets the bleed-off amount according to the control input detected by the pressure sensors (40 and 41) and, based on the set bleed-off amount, controls the opening area of the cut valve (36) so as to suppress a shock caused at the time of abrupt swing operation.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Dispositif de commande hydraulique d'une machine de chantier, qui commande le débit et le sens d'écoulement de l'huile sous pression évacuée de la pompe hydraulique (20) par une soupape de commande (27) avant que l'huile soit envoyée à un moteur oscillant (4). Ledit dispositif est caractérisé en ce qu'il comporte une voie de purge (33) d'huile destinée à la purge d'une partie de l'huile sous pression apportée au moteur oscillant (4), une vanne d'arrêt (36) installée dans la voie de purge (33) d'huile, qui régule la quantité d'huile purgée, un dispositif de commande (42) qui commande la vanne d'arrêt (36) à l'aide d'une vanne proportionnelle électromagnétique (37), et des capteurs de pression (40, 41) qui détectent la commande d'entrée d'une soupape (39) télécommandée du mouvement d'oscillation. Le dispositif de commande (42) règle la quantité de purge en fonction de la commande d'entrée détectée par les capteurs de pression (40, 41) et, sur la base de la quantité de purge fixée, commande la zone d'ouverture de la vanne d'arrêt (36) de manière à éliminer le choc provoqué au moment d'une opération soudaine d'oscillation.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>